  "body": "### What is the issue with the DOM Standard?\n\nAfter #1079, the following parts of the spec will still reference XML name stuff:\n\n- `createProcessingInstruction()` checks against the XML `Name` production\n- `createDocumentType()` checks against the XML Namespaces `QName` production\n\n(Additionally, there are historical references to the `Char` and `Name` production, and how we _don't_ validate against them.)\n\nI suspect in both cases you can create PIs/doctypes that violate these rules using the HTML parser, so we could consider doing something similar to #1079.\n\nHowever, the priority here is significantly lower than for attributes and elements.",
